# Networking Task

Task: Create a VLAN interface named `{{vlan_iface}}` with VLAN ID `{{vlan_id}}` on top of the network interface `{{nic}}`, and assign it the address `{{vlan_ip}}`.

- The interface `{{vlan_iface}}` must exist, be up, and carry the address `{{vlan_ip}}`.
- It must be tagged with VLAN ID `{{vlan_id}}` and be attached to `{{nic}}`.
- Persist the configuration in a new dedicated configuration file; do not overwrite or delete any existing network configuration files.
- Do not modify the configuration of any other network interface, and do not change the system default route.
- The configuration must persist across reboots.
